  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Close accepted M4-W01-C01-T2 after executing 14 independent .NET 10 AngouriMath 2.5.0 host/worker checks. Bound a fixed two-expression corpus with input length, nesting and token caps; retain observable x!=1 conditions; refuse unknown real/complex assumptions. Verify explicit child failure, real cancellation signal and timed process-tree termination, plus the exact observed T1 MIT package SHA-256 and relevant Math IR/quantity regressions.",
    "value": "Establish a truthful, bounded symbolic-provider integration boundary without claiming a public Math CAS, native cooperative cancellation, a general-purpose sandbox, translated IR assumptions or AURA broker support.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "One package-isolated C# host executes a fourteen-probe scientific corpus and launches only fixed child modes; no new product symbolic project, provider runtime or user-supplied commands are admitted.",
      "Input refusal is explicit for overlong, overly nested, over-token-budget, malformed and unsupported mathematical expressions; real sqrt(x^2) assumptions remain unresolved.",
      "Angouri's previously observed condition-bearing cancellation is rechecked without interpreting its string as typed Math IR; x=1 remains excluded by the independent fixed-corpus input policy.",
      "The host demonstrably terminates a sleeping child on a finite deadline and CancellationTokenSource signal; cooperative CAS cancellation, a secure sandbox and CPU/memory quotas remain unqualified.",
      "The pinned Angouri 2.5.0 restored archive is independently reidentified against RS053's observed MIT SHA-256 and five direct dependency identities.",
      "Existing quantity and IR regression tests, locked Math solution build, product/native planning projections and transfer architecture remain trusted.",
      "C01-T2 A/B/C, T2 and C01 close with evidence; M4 and M4-W01 stay in progress, C02 remains not-ready, and no AURA/Decision/MCDM/dw.discovery adoption is asserted."
    ],
    "nextAction": "After durable RS054 success, prepare M4-W01-C02-T1 controlled RED/GREEN for a typed symbolic IR bridge preserving x!=1 exclusions and refusing unrepresentable provider predicates.",
    "achievements": [
      {
        "projectNode": "M4-W01-C01-T2-A",
        "achievement": "Fix accepted provider containment, conservative closed-corpus admission, host deadline/cancellation and unrepresentable symbolic-assumption refusal boundaries."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M4-W01-C01-T2-B",
        "achievement": "Execute 14 independent source-backed host/worker probes, pinned Angouri NuGet identity verification, relevant Math IR/quantity regression and structural checks."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M4-W01-C01-T2-C",
        "achievement": "Record the distinction between provider conditional text, unsupported typed Math IR, host termination versus cooperative CAS cancellation, and unqualified sandbox/platform behavior."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M4-W01-C01-T2",
        "achievement": "Complete C01-T2 as an observed bounded symbolic-process host and mathematical-domain refusal study, with no public symbolic adapter or broker admission."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M4-W01-C01",
        "achievement": "Close M4-W01-C01 after T1's two-provider qualification and T2's 14-probe host/budget boundary evidence, preserving M4-W01/C02 as unfinished."
      }
    ]
  },
